// Where one value sits relative to another.
//
// A three-way answer rather than two `Bool` calls: `a < b` and `b < a` asks the
// comparison twice and leaves "equal" to be inferred from both being false,
// which is one place for a hand-written comparison to disagree with itself.
//
// This is the type the compiler's native `compare(a, b)` answers — the whole
// three-way order of any value whose shape carries one, with no `@Derive`. It
// lives here as an ordinary Foundation type, not behind a macro, because the
// comparison that produces it is the compiler's own.
enum Ordering {
    Less
    Equal
    Greater
}
